       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation can't stand in for a clinician's review.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the ordering physician or prescriber to review the order. If they really intend a dose above the maximum, they can enter it themselves and discuss it with pharmacy.\n- If the dose was a typo, send me the corrected dose and a clinician's confirmation. For example, 100 mg or 200 mg once daily would be within the normal range.\n- If this is for a financial or billing analysis, you don't need a live order. I can help you in some other way that doesn't involve a patient order."
